WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.140
Stir fresh pineapple into gelatin and chill it, and the gelatin can stay runny.

2
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.800
Use canned pineapple, and it sets.

3
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.300
Gelatin is a protein.

4
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:19.500
When it cools, its long chains tangle into a net that traps water.

5
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.640
What is in fresh pineapple, and what did canning change?

6
00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:29.113
Metabolism means all the chemical reactions in a living thing.

7
00:00:29.953 --> 00:00:33.633
Many would be far too slow at body temperature without help.

8
00:00:34.473 --> 00:00:40.193
The help comes from enzymes, almost all of them proteins, that speed up specific

9
00:00:40.193 --> 00:00:43.473
reactions. An enzyme is a catalyst.

10
00:00:44.113 --> 00:00:47.093
It speeds up a reaction without being used up.

11
00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:51.363
Take catalase, an enzyme in potato cells.

12
00:00:52.143 --> 00:00:55.703
The substrate is the molecule an enzyme acts on.

13
00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:58.683
For catalase, that is hydrogen peroxide.

14
00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:03.983
The substrate fits into the active site, a small pocket on the enzyme.

15
00:01:04.543 --> 00:01:08.483
The enzyme changes it into products, water and oxygen.

16
00:01:09.283 --> 00:01:10.283
The products leave.

17
00:01:10.763 --> 00:01:14.363
The enzyme is unchanged and can take in another substrate molecule.

18
00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:18.427
Picture a ball that must be pushed over a hill.

19
00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:24.347
Activation energy is the energy needed to get a reaction started, like that hill.

20
00:01:25.147 --> 00:01:27.347
An enzyme does not add energy.

21
00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:31.827
It holds the substrate where bonds break or form more easily.

22
00:01:32.387 --> 00:01:36.327
That lowers the hill, so more substrate reacts each second.

23
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:44.140
Warmer molecules move faster, so up to a point a warmer reaction runs faster.

24
00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:50.020
But too much heat shakes apart the weak attractions that hold the folded chain in

25
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:55.600
shape. To denature is to lose the folded shape a protein needs to work.

26
00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.100
A denatured enzyme is not dead, but its active site no longer fits.

27
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.580
The optimum is the condition where an enzyme works fastest.

28
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:10.280
Most human enzymes have an optimum near 37 °C.

29
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.500
Each enzyme also has a best pH.

30
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:21.400
A change in pH changes electric charges, so substrate and active site may no longer

31
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.600
attract. Back to the pineapple.

32
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.480
Fresh pineapple contains bromelain, an enzyme that cuts the protein chains in

33
00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.920
gelatin. Canning heats the fruit enough to denature bromelain.

34
00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.800
So the canned gelatin sets.

35
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.420
The rule: an enzyme works only while its active site keeps its shape.
